A||||8||Leadfoot||Engine wiring pics||||5||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-05-2001||05:54 PM||||About a week ago I started to hear a knocking noise coming from my 2.8 (150K miles).  I thought I could ride it in that condition for at least a week but 20 miles later the engine just quit and wouldn't turn-over since then.  So I tore the engine apart and found that the #3 connecting rod bearing was gone!  YIKES!  I have just rebuilt the engine and was wondering if anyone has any pics showing the correct way to route the wires.  Darn it! I knew I should have bought that digital camera.  Would the service manual have that?  Maybe I should by one of those too.  Thanks! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||06-05-2001||06:31 PM||||It wouldn't hurt to get the helms book.... <P>Most of the wiring will only fit in a limited number of ways. As long as you don't lay something on the exhaust you can't go too awfull wrong with it. Most connectors only fit what they belong on so it's pretty hard to mess up. Easiest thing is to lay the harness out on top of/around the engine... It will tell you where it wants to go in most cases.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-05-2001||06:37 PM||||I have both the chilton and hanyes manuals but they give limited info.  I think I stop by the local junk yard and see if I can find a 2.8 (maybe even find a 120 speedo).  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Firebug||06-05-2001||07:18 PM||||I would also like to see wiring pics...  I am converting a four cylinder car to a 2.8 and I have got a wiring harness in a box.  The engine is almost complete on the stand, but the wiring would be very helpful with a pic for hints.  As they say, they say a thousand words.  If someone has a v-6 on the floor in their garage, that would be perfect.<P>Thanks alot for your time...<BR>Scott||||reg||10
